---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Methodology — How RestAreaNearMe Sources Stops" description="How a rest area gets listed, what counts as verified, and what we refuse to publish.">
  <section class="wrap hero"><h1 class="h1">Methodology</h1></section>
  <section class="wrap section">
    <p class="lede">A stop is listed only when it can be sourced.</p>
    <h2 class="h2">Sources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>NHAI published wayside-amenity lists.</li>
      <li>OpenStreetMap, for facilities tagged as services, rest areas or fuel with toilets.</li>
      <li>Reader submissions, reviewed before publishing.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="h2">What we will not publish</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A coordinate we have not verified.</li>
      <li>An opening time we have not confirmed — it shows as “not published”.</li>
      <li>An amenity inferred from the operator's brand.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each row shows its source and the date it was last verified.</p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding: clamp(1.8rem, 5vw, 3rem) 0 0.5rem; }
  .section { padding: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem; max-width: 46rem; }
  .section p, .section li { line-height: 1.65; color: var(--color-ink-soft); }
  .section h2 { margin-top: 1.8rem; }
</style>
